New is used to allocate memory for a new zeroed value
of a specified type.
New is generally used with struct 

Make is used to initialize maps, list and channels in 
GoLang
Without initialization, you won't be able to use these (maps, list and 
channels properly)

Why Initialization Is Required for These Types
Slices need an underlying array and a descriptor pointing to it.
Maps need an internal hash table for storing key-value pairs.
Channels need internal buffers and synchronization mechanisms for communication.

====
This panics because we didn't initialize the map
var m map[string]int // nil map
m["Alice"] = 25       // Panic: assignment to entry in nil map
====
In this example, it doesn't panic because after you declare a nil map
you then initialized it 

var m map[string]int // This is a nil map

// Initialize manually (with a loop or direct assignment)
m = map[string]int{} // Manually create the map

m["Alice"] = 25
m["Bob"] = 30
